    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "Photographs of fluke's ventral surface of humpback whales (Megaptera\nnovaeangliae) were taken in Bransfield and Gerlache Strait, near Antarctic\nPeninsula, during four summers seasons (1994/95, 1995/96, 1996/97 and 1997/98).\nThese photos permit identification of each individual with the objective of\nknowing local distribution and movements and long-distance movements between\nwinter and summer grounds. Up to the present, we have identified approximately\n150 humpbacks whales in this manner, knowing local movements within the same\nseason of a few and without re-capture between summers seasons.",
